# Safe change and regression

1. Inspect before editing; find the **source of truth** first.
2. Do not create parallel implementations of an existing workflow.
3. Do not UI-only-patch a backend-state bug; do not prompt-only-patch a deterministic rule.
4. No unrelated refactoring during a targeted fix; keep diffs small.
5. Preserve public interfaces unless migration is explicitly requested.
6. Every production defect fix needs a regression test. Never delete tests to green a change.
7. Do not weaken type safety; no unjustified `any`, unsafe casts, or swallowed errors.
8. Do not report completion before relevant checks; never fabricate results. If a command cannot run, say so.
9. Before editing shared/global code, identify affected agencies, clinics, and flows.
10. **Product-global** changes: test at least one Agency Portal flow and one Clinic Portal / single-clinic flow when applicable (include FeelinHealthy when that surface is affected); guest and authenticated when applicable.
11. Regression-sensitive: consent, intake, lead, quote, appointment, Prompt Studio, conversation records.
